// The workspace ties the library to the tools module beside it, so that `go
// build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` from the repository root still
// reach every package in the repository, and an edit to the library is seen by
// the tools without a version to bump.
//
// It is committed deliberately. Nothing consuming this repository as a dependency
// reads it — a workspace applies to the tree you are working in, not to a module
// someone downloads — so it costs a consumer nothing.
go 1.26.5

use (
	.
	./tools
)
